 "result": "I created two files in the repository root. I could not build or run the image, so both are checked by reading the code only.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`**: a two-stage build.\n  - **Build:** `golang:1.26` compiles `./cmd/server` with `CGO_ENABLED=0`. The frontend is embedded, so the binary is self-contained.\n  - **Runtime:** `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot`, which runs as non-root. I picked it because the app makes outbound HTTPS calls to registries and distroless includes CA certificates.\n  - It listens on `PORT` (default 8080), exposed and set in the image. Secrets like `AUTH_KEY` are passed at runtime, not baked in.\n- **`.dockerignore`**: excludes VCS and editor metadata, build outputs, `.env*` files, `.vercel`, `node_modules`, and `alicia-notes`.\n\nChoices you may want to change:\n- The Makefile's `docker` target already runs `docker build` with `.`, so it should work now. It doesn't pass a version, so the image reports `version=dev` unless you add `--build-arg VERSION=...`.\n- Base images use tags, not digests, so they can drift. Pin digests if you need reproducible builds.\n- I did not add a `HEALTHCHECK`, because distroless has no shell, `curl`, or `wget` to run one.",
